  {
   "slug": "speech-826712",
   "speaker": "Arthur Sinodinos",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-12-11",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker presented the Environment Legislation Amendment Bill 2013 to provide legal certainty for past conservation decisions under the EPBC Act and triple criminal and civil penalties for poaching and illegal trade of turtles and dugong. The Infrastructure Australia Amendment Bill 2013 was introduced to restructure the agency as an independent authority, conduct five-yearly audits, develop a 15-year infrastructure plan, and review all Commonwealth-funded projects over $100 million. The Migration Amendment (Regaining Control Over Australia’s Protection Obligations) Bill 2013 removes the complementary protection criterion from the Migration Act, reverting to an administrative process for assessing non-refoulement obligations under the CAT and ICCPR, while maintaining those obligations."
  },
